# leak-deny.sha256 — sha256 of lowercase tokens that must never appear in the public tree.
# One lowercase hex digest per line; `#` starts a comment. The words themselves are NOT stored here:
# scripts/ci-leakguard.mjs (rule `denied-token`) splits every scanned line into tokens
# ([a-z0-9][a-z0-9.-]*[a-z0-9]), takes each token, each of its dot-suffixes and every contiguous run
# of dash/dot-separated labels, hashes them with sha256 and looks the digest up here.
# A hit prints only file:line and the first 8 hex of the digest — never the token.
# To deny a new word: printf %s 'word' | shasum -a 256, and append the digest (lowercase, no word nearby).
